{"brief": "为 XGO Duck 设计一个友好、有辨识度的头顶外观装饰件，具体视觉主题由你决定。保留原机器人和相机，不做尖锐或夸张笨重的造型。希望它作为个性化可打印原型展示；安装方式和真实运动性能仍待验证。请根据实际整机与近景渲染进行有限轮审查和修改。", "eligible": [{"round": 0, "review": {"recipe_sha256": "47de11472e44efcaba67d3dd13883d7764d2f1c8a084a533835950e425600c8b", "verdict": "needs-review", "findings": ["Build is host-eligible: proof accepted, motion passed at all 31 poses with min distance 16.8 mm, single fused solid, added mass 0.88 g — no floating or disconnected geometry in the CAD facts.", "Close-up renders show the crest sits cleanly on the head-top rear slope, forward of the rear edge, and does not intrude on the camera lens or front dome in any of the four views.", "Problem: at 14x12x2.5 base with 6-8 mm puffs, the part reads as a tiny yellow speck in the whole-robot views (barely visible in perspective and -Y view). It fails the brief's '有辨识度' (recognizable) requirement — the silhouette is too timid relative to the large head dome.", "The three-puff 'duckling tuft' idea is coherent and friendly (no sharp edges), but at this scale it reads as a generic bump rather than a crest; the top view shows it as a small dot far from the head apex, weakening the identity claim.", "No obstruction found: the part is far from the lens (front of head) and clear of all source geometry; zone compliance confirmed by bbox within 80x80x35 mm.", "Revision direction: scale the puff cluster up modestly (center puff ~14x11x9 mm) and shift it closer to the head apex so it is clearly visible from front and side views, while keeping lowest-Z overlap with the 2.5 mm base and staying soft/rounded per the friendly brief.", "Attachment remains an adhesive-pad proposal only; interface_status is unverified and walking/printability remain open, as the brief acknowledges."], "next_step": "revise", "reason": "The candidate is structurally sound, connected and non-obstructive, and its friendly rounded styling matches the brief. However, the whole-robot renders show it is far too small and rear-placed to be recognizable as an identity feature on the XGO Duck's large head — it reads as a barely visible speck. A limited revision will enlarge and reposition the puff cluster for presence while preserving the accepted overlap, zone and motion-clearance margins."}, "candidate": {"directory": "/home/exuber/CODE/CORE/pythonProject1/AUTORESEARCH/fluxkernel/.demo/v010-personalization/robot-pal-6985339a/round-00/xgoduck-part-af8c6994", "native_sha256": "e6e328746f41a05a5894c6ec77f29180c340baa041317e790564992f390a5ab2", "name": "xgoduck", "bodies": 16, "joints": 15, "actuators": 14, "meshes": 16, "mass_kg": 0.800876800147657, "proof_accepted": true, "deployment_ready": false, "accepted": true, "motion_passed": true, "motion_summary": {"minimum_distance_m": 0.016773138372725746, "violations": []}, "part_body": "custom_duckling_crest_puff", "added_mass_kg": 0.0008768108476570091, "interface_status": "unverified", "recipe_sha256": "47de11472e44efcaba67d3dd13883d7764d2f1c8a084a533835950e425600c8b"}}, {"round": 2, "review": {"recipe_sha256": "73fa5dc7fbff117625e004bce5722f34396e1c41d1f165bfcff9794a95a2c409", "verdict": "meets-brief", "findings": ["Whole-robot renders (perspective, -Y, +X, top) show the yellow two-puff crest sitting centered on the head-top dome, clearly visible and recognizable without obscuring the front camera lens or face dome.", "Close-up renders confirm a soft, rounded, friendly silhouette; no sharp or intimidating edges, matching the brief.", "Scale is compact: bbox ~18x16x11.8 mm, well inside the 80x80x35 mm zone; added mass ~2.15 g, far under budget; nothing implausibly large or obstructive.", "Part is a single fused solid (solids: 1); center puff (15x12x10, -10 deg X tilt) and bilateral side puffs (10x6x7, -15 deg X tilt) all embed within the 3 mm base with positive-volume overlap; no floating geometry; no material below Z=0 (lowest feature Z ~+1.43 mm).", "Build proof accepted (proof_accepted: true), motion check passed across 31 poses with minimum distance ~16.1 mm vs 0.2 mm tolerance; no collisions with original visible geometry.", "CAD-vs-STEP volume discrepancy from round 1 resolved by simplifying to two ellipsoids with single-axis rotations; reported volume 1732.9 mm3 is consistent with the recipe digest.", "Camera, electronics, shells and joints untouched; only one connected decorative part added on the fixed head-top datum.", "Interface status remains unverified and adhesive attachment, curvature fit, printability and real walking performance are explicitly open, consistent with prototype-study framing."], "next_step": "stop", "reason": "Round-2 candidate duckling_crest_puff_mk2c builds cleanly (proof accepted, single solid), passes sampled motion clearance, and the actual whole-robot and close-up renders show a friendly, recognizable rounded crest on the head top that preserves the XGO Duck identity and camera view. The prior volume-mismatch concern was addressed by simplifying geometry. Remaining unknowns (mount, fit, printing, gait) are declared open by the brief and do not block selection of this built, reviewed, eligible round."}, "candidate": {"directory": "/home/exuber/CODE/CORE/pythonProject1/AUTORESEARCH/fluxkernel/.demo/v010-personalization/robot-pal-6985339a/round-02/xgoduck-part-0610b949", "native_sha256": "4a5f6cebb373e2ad8d8f5b3cd4f4692c264f356ad347cdce5a7f2b8dcd29f161", "name": "xgoduck", "bodies": 16, "joints": 15, "actuators": 14, "meshes": 16, "mass_kg": 0.8021487726055273, "proof_accepted": true, "deployment_ready": false, "accepted": true, "motion_passed": true, "motion_summary": {"minimum_distance_m": 0.01606420654253603, "violations": []}, "part_body": "custom_duckling_crest_puff_mk2c", "added_mass_kg": 0.0021487833055272654, "interface_status": "unverified", "recipe_sha256": "73fa5dc7fbff117625e004bce5722f34396e1c41d1f165bfcff9794a95a2c409"}}]}
